    "summary": "SPF measures how well sunscreen blocks UVB rays, but the difference between SPF 30 and SPF 100 is only about 1–2% in actual protection. Most dermatologists recommend broad-spectrum SPF 30–50, with consistent and generous reapplication being more important than a higher SPF number.",
